VIDEO_GENERATION_WORKFLOW_HELP = "# Start with the video goal and exact source\n\nChoose the intended task, exact model family/version and supported role, output dimensions, frame/time choices and source-image transform. A catalog entry or a compatible-looking filename is not executable support. Source/reference identity, requested output and observed generated timing retain separate evidence. Optional local video does not block ordinary offline image collection.\n\n## Keep saved drafts and local setup separate\n\nA video draft records authored choices; local setup records runtime/model configuration. Neither is a submitted job or verified generated output. Save a changed draft to a new JSON file; existing drafts are not silently overwritten. Review the intended filename and original source again if choices change during a picker.\n\nLoading or starting a new draft can require Save/Discard/Cancel for changed work. **Read Guide…** or F1 declines that prompt: it saves neither draft nor setup, discards neither, and grants no reset or execution consent. Existing saved files remain separate from the current unsaved workspace. Finish reading, then deliberately choose the original action again.\n\n## Review setup and prepared model storage\n\nChoose exact registered model files and supported runtime paths. Preview setup, prepared model-storage review and runtime start are distinct stages. Missing resources, credentials, physical layout or native qualification stay held; a recommendation or machine-fit estimate does not establish actual usability or output quality. The resource-preparation guide explains its separate copy/cleanup/retained-process decisions.\n\nPreparing a runtime or saving local setup does not submit a video job. Runtime start and model acquisition/install retain their existing explicit consent, identity checks, recovery and process owner. This guidance does not qualify or start them.\n\n## Prepare, review and submit one original request\n\nPrepare binds the exact draft/source/models/runtime and output plan. Inspect readiness, memory guidance and held reasons before Submit. A changed request, source, boundary or runtime requires current review rather than silently adopting a different job. Runtime fit/speed is separate from generated quality. Cancel Step, Cancel Job and owned-runtime stop keep their original service responsibilities; accepted work and recovery receipts remain with those owners.\n\nA submitted, completed, retained or verified result has a different next action. Review the original exact result before retrying an uncertain submission or recovery. Stop/recovery must use the exact owned runtime/process evidence; do not adopt another process or bypass an uncertain-start hold.\n\n## Review and finish verified outputs separately\n\nPreview verifies/decodes through its own owner. Finishing creates separate exact extracted frames or trims. Sending a verified result to Ingest starts the normal unreviewed transfer/admission review; it does not silently confirm image facts. Remix/Animate use a separately rechecked frame lineage to prepare a new draft, not automatically generate one.\n\nClose can hide this workspace while owned work continues. Reopen it to monitor, stop or recover that same work; hiding is not cancellation, physical process death or completed shutdown. Final application shutdown drains exact owned work through the existing coordinator. Native/source-owner/packaged acceptance remains separately unqualified.\n\n\n## Read without replaying the operation\n\n**Help** or **F1** opens this exact guide; **Learning Library** provides the offline article, bookmarks and independent Learning Notes. **Save Note** saves reading, not a draft, setup, video, transfer, pack, runtime or consent. Failed saves retain their draft. Settle notes and reading searches before fresh actions or Close. Changed sources/choices or a new reader hold the request. Finish reading and choose again; refused actions do not replay. Modeless reading keeps existing Pause/Cancel/owned stop actions reachable.\n\n## Source scope\n\nThis guide describes the CollectiGen source snapshot dated 2026-11-01. Native execution and installed-package behavior remain separately unqualified. Reading guidance changes no Image Knowledge. Reading notes, source access, saved choices and permission to run or share remain separate. Follow the workflow's displayed readiness, consent, saved-result and recovery controls.\n"

